<resources>
    <!-- ===================== System accent (Android 12+) =====================
         The only overlay that has no literals: every value is a framework tone, and the framework
         rewrites those tones per user when the wallpaper/Material You palette changes (Runtime Resource
         Overlays on the android package). Resolution happens when a view reads `?attr/accentColor`, so
         the app follows the OS palette without holding a color of its own.

         The tones are chosen for an AMOLED surface, not for Material's light-background roles:
         400 is bright enough to read as an accent on pure black, 200 is its lighter partner, and the
         two alpha attributes cannot reference a tone *with* alpha — XML has no way to blend a color
         resource — so the low-alpha stroke takes the darkest usable tone (800) and the badge fill the
         next step below the solid (600), which is what 14 % and 80 % of the solid looked like over black.
         AccentPalette.isSystemAccentAvailable keeps this style away from a device that would resolve
         the tones to nothing usable.

         The tonal ramp the onboarding illustrations are drawn in follows the same ladder: 300 is the
         bright tile, 100 the pale caption, and 600/700/900 the three steps down that a multi-panel
         scene needs to keep its depth without the app holding a color of its own. -->
    <style name="Accent.System">
        <item name="accentColor">@android:color/system_accent1_400</item>
        <item name="accentColorLight">@android:color/system_accent1_200</item>
        <item name="accentColorAlpha14">@android:color/system_accent1_800</item>
        <item name="accentColorAlpha80">@android:color/system_accent1_600</item>
        <item name="accentColorBright">@android:color/system_accent1_300</item>
        <item name="accentColorMuted">@android:color/system_accent1_100</item>
        <item name="accentColorDark">@android:color/system_accent1_600</item>
        <item name="accentColorDarker">@android:color/system_accent1_700</item>
        <item name="accentColorDeep">@android:color/system_accent1_900</item>
        <item name="colorAccent">@android:color/system_accent1_400</item>
    </style>
</resources>
